1
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:01,400
Tri.

2
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:03,720
Sasi.

3
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,800
Is she just another friend,
like Ms. Srichan?

4
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,120
She's my ex-fiancée.

5
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,479
<i>Are you secretly seeing Tri?</i>

6
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:12,000
<i>We're uncle and niece.</i>

7
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:14,160
Who would think that way?

8
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,560
What if he weren't your uncle?

9
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,440
Would you?

10
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:22,920
<i>After leaving the Som Song Saeng house,</i>
<i>I'm working for…</i>

11
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,840
Freeze! Don't move!

12
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,840
You're slower than I expected.

13
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,600
Did you forget we're in the jungle?

14
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,640
We have guns too, you fool!

15
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,080
Move out! Let's go!

16
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,840
I dare you to try and shoot me, Thatri!

17
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,520
How was it, Boss? Did my smoke bombs
help you crush Thatri?

18
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:40,000
Thanks a lot. Without your help,
it wouldn't have been this easy.

19
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:45,120
So… did you finish him off for me?

20
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:46,880
Not yet.

21
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:50,640
Why not? I literally told you
how to double-cross them.

22
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:54,760
A pathetic loser like Thatri
can be dealt with at any time.

23
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,120
Now, the loot and the money
are far more important.

24
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,120
-But I want Thatri dead.
-Hey!

25
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:05,000
I know you're itching for vengeance.

26
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:06,400
Don't you worry.

27
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,560
I'll help you get your revenge.

28
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:10,720
I despise him just as much as you do.

29
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,000
But right now, the money comes first!

30
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,720
Understood, Boss.

31
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:17,360
Move out, boys.

32
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,200
If last night's stress
is ruining your appetite,

33
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:51,400
at least have some of this
Bak Kut Teh broth.

34
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,160
Thank you.

35
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:11,840
The broth is so fragrant,

36
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,840
and the pork ribs are incredibly tender.

37
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,360
It's really delicious.

38
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:26,400
There's no need to force it.

39
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:28,280
I'll eat when I feel like it.

40
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:32,000
If you don't eat it,
I'm going to be really upset.

41
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,360
I cooked this all by myself.

42
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:56,840
Look who said they couldn't eat.

43
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,440
You cleaned out the entire pot.

44
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,000
You worked so hard on it,

45
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:06,080
so I had to finish it all.
I was just being polite, you know.

46
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,800
Are you feeling less stressed now?

47
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:13,520
It's all thanks to you.

48
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,200
It really was delicious.

49
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,280
I'll make it for you again sometime.

50
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,840
Mr. Thatri, the District Chief
is here to see you.

51
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,760
Alright.

52
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:32,560
If I'd been there, I never would've let
Zhang Gong Cheng pull off that raid.

53
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:36,640
No, I botched the plan.

54
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:40,400
I didn't think Zhang Gong Cheng
would be clever enough to outsmart us.

55
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:44,760
We must be far more cautious from now on.

56
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:47,960
Otherwise, Colonel Nakamura
will be in serious trouble.

57
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:54,160
What did you go to Bangkok for,
District Chief?

58
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,160
I went there to get married.

59
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,360
-What? Married?
-What? Married?

60
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,360
Yes.

61
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:07,240
You didn't say a word.
I would've gone to celebrate with you.

62
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,800
For an auspicious event like this,
you should've told us.

63
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:12,760
Well…

64
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:17,160
I felt that the Japanese transportation
was far more critical than my own wedding.

65
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:20,840
With people's lives on the line,
I couldn't be reckless

66
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:24,760
and have you and Colonel Nakamura
leave to Bangkok with me.

67
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:28,440
Right. The timing clashed perfectly.

68
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:29,680
Yes,

69
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:32,280
and it was a last-minute wedding.

70
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:35,440
I didn't inform anyone,
except for my immediate family.

71
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,440
So, who is the bride?

72
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:39,280
Why don't you bring her here?

73
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:42,480
Leaving her behind after the wedding,
she must be terribly lonely.

74
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:46,240
Of course not, I brought her with me.

75
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:50,200
She should be taking a stroll
in the front garden right now.

76
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,920
Oh.

77
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,440
Here she is. Honey…

78
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,200
Tri?

79
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,760
Sasi?

80
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,160
Now that you two are married,

81
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:23,440
talk things out nicely
and lean on each other, dear.

82
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:25,880
Yes, Mother.

83
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:29,320
Please look after my daughter for me.

84
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,280
I will, Mother.

85
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:06,160
I didn't make it myself this time.
I bought this one.

86
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:08,240
What is it?

87
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:14,480
It's Bee Tai Bak,
a traditional Phuket dessert.

88
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:16,160
The noodles are white and red,

89
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,720
unlike the green Thai Lod Chong.

90
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:20,920
There's no coconut milk,

91
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,280
and best of all,

92
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:24,880
it has a beautiful scent
of jasmine-infused water.

93
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:27,880
Right. I don't want any.

94
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:30,760
Please have some.

95
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:33,200
You can tell it's delicious

96
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:35,320
just from the jasmine aroma.

97
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:40,520
Even if you shove it down my throat,
I have absolutely no appetite.

98
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,000
Not since I saw Sasi.

99
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:50,080
You don't need to eat it then.
I'll eat it myself.

100
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,480
This is absolutely delicious.

101
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:08,840
It's so aromatic.

102
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,440
Well then, I'm leaving now.

103
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:31,160
Sure, go on then.

104
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:59,280
Is this for me, Sasi?

105
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:01,600
Yes.

106
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:05,000
I know how much pain you're in,

107
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:08,640
losing both of your parents like this.

108
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,200
But I want you to be strong

109
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:14,920
and find a way to get through this.

110
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,840
And will you stay by my side

111
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:24,000
so we can get through it together?

112
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,640
Of course I will.

113
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,400
Let me get this straight.

114
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:34,440
I want you to break off the engagement.

115
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,560
I'm so sorry.

116
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,560
DISTRICT CHIEF'S RESIDENCE

117
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,280
Even if your fiancé isn't rich,

118
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:03,680
he has a bright future ahead.

119
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:05,800
And above all,

120
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,560
he loves you deeply.

121
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:10,400
Otherwise, he wouldn't have waited
for you for ten years.

122
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:14,600
That just makes me feel
even more like a terrible person.

123
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,120
To survive,

124
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:20,040
we didn't just deceive Tri,

125
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,600
-but also--
-Enough, Sasi!

126
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,360
Hey.

127
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,400
Yes?

128
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,200
What are you thinking about?

129
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:36,760
Are you homesick?

130
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:40,320
Yes.

131
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,400
Would you like to go out somewhere?

132
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:48,040
I'd rather not.
It's been a tiring journey today.

133
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,920
I don't feel like going anywhere.

134
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,600
Phuket has so many beautiful places.

135
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,440
I'll take you around sometime.

136
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:57,040
Alright.

137
00:12:57,120 --> 00:13:00,760
Oh, and the library here is massive.

138
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,080
You're going to love it.

139
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,000
Right nearby,

140
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:09,040
there's an O-aew dessert shop
and a traditional Kopi Tiam coffee house.

141
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,120
Should I take you there?

142
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:14,840
That sounds nice.

143
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,920
Are you hungry?
Let me go prepare some food for you.

144
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:22,000
Please wait a moment.

145
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,520
Still heartbroken, huh?

146
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,920
Hmph.

147
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:50,280
Oh, Don Jose, my baby.

148
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,160
What are you doing here, boy?

149
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:22,640
Take this to your owner for me.

150
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,360
What did you bring me, Don Jose?

151
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,560
<i>Starving yourself over a broken heart,</i>

152
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:47,960
<i>you might die from hunger.</i>

153
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:10,160
Take this right back to your mother.

154
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:25,760
<i>I'm not heartbroken.</i>

155
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,040
<i>Just felt uneasy.</i>

156
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,480
Not heartbroken, huh?

157
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:47,480
Another note already?

158
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:55,400
<i>In that case, stop frowning so much.</i>

159
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:57,600
<i>You already have too many wrinkles anyway.</i>

160
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,960
Let's see what it says…

161
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:11,800
<i>You talk big now,</i>
<i>just you wait until you get old yourself,</i>

162
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:13,320
<i>stubborn girl.</i>

163
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:26,400
Don't get tired on me now, Don Jose.

164
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,440
Get up first, boy.

165
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,240
Mr. Thatri.

166
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,960
Colonel Nakamura is here to see you.

167
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,600
Oh.

168
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:45,320
Colonel Nakamura,
what brings you all the way here?

169
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,040
Is there an urgent matter?

170
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,640
We finally have a lead

171
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,920
on where the items are being sold.

172
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:56,320
So, our plan worked out after all.

173
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,920
All the items sold by Mr. Khom

174
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,960
were definitely stolen
from the Japanese the other day.

175
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,200
I dare you to try and shoot me, Thatri!

176
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,560
Woo!

177
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,800
These items were all scattered
across the black market.

178
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,560
My men went undercover,

179
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,040
so we were able to buy them back.

180
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:31,800
Spit it out!

181
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:35,840
Who did you buy these goods from?

182
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:38,560
My shop sells only legal items.

183
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,960
I never buy stolen goods.

184
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:43,000
You'd better stop framing me.

185
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:46,520
I take it you're asking for proof?

186
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:06,120
Mark the goods and let them take it.

187
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,840
Then we track them down

188
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:10,960
to get the stuff back and take them out.

189
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,280
Very meticulous.

190
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:17,320
But I am slightly curious, Thatri-san.

191
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,920
Since Mr. Wai is already your informant,

192
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:24,200
why didn't you just raid them right away?

193
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:30,000
I thought so too at first.

194
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:33,160
But Wai said they constantly move,

195
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,240
sometimes on the mainland,
sometimes on the islands.

196
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,960
Only when selling the goods
do they stay in one place

197
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,200
to distribute them to buyers.

198
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:45,320
That's the best time to strike.

199
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:49,040
Besides,

200
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:52,480
I want to wipe out the whole ring.

201
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,360
If we don't root them out,

202
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:55,760
they will strike again.

203
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:57,960
That's why I marked the items.

204
00:18:58,040 --> 00:19:01,400
Catching them with the evidence,
they'll have no way out,

205
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:03,640
forcing them to turn on each other.

206
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,400
This is the liquor seized
from Mr. Khom's shop.

207
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:33,880
And these are the markings our men made.

208
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:37,360
Oh!

209
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:40,720
You know exactly how the Japanese military

210
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:43,520
executes those who steal from our army,

211
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,320
don't you?

212
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,560
I confess!

213
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:53,240
Please don't hurt me. I confess.

214
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:55,360
I surrender. Please don't hurt me.

215
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:57,080
Then tell us everything.

216
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,880
Who are your people,
and how do you operate?

217
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,840
I'll turn you into a protected witness.

218
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:03,360
Yes, yes!

219
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,640
I'll tell you

220
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:08,000
about everyone involved.
Just please don't hurt me.

221
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:10,840
I surrender. Please spare me.

222
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:26,200
What are you doing with that gun?

223
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:30,400
It's nothing. Just making sure
I'm fully prepared.

224
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:09,640
You smell wonderful.

225
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,600
I'm sorry…

226
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,000
It's alright.

227
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,920
Since we got married,

228
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:58,720
I've never fulfilled my duties as a wife.

229
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:02,400
You can be mad at me.

230
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:09,480
I told you, it's fine.

231
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:12,800
Don't overthink it.

232
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:15,080
I understand completely.

233
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:59,440
ADISUAN PEARLS

234
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:02,560
I invested so much
in robbing the Japanese.

235
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:04,560
Why are the profits so low?!

236
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:06,840
Someone is undercutting us.

237
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:09,320
I don't know where they sourced
their black-market goods,

238
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,920
but their prices are half of ours.

239
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,480
Everyone is buying from them,

240
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:15,360
so we had to lower prices
and lose profits.

241
00:23:15,880 --> 00:23:18,200
And you still haven't found

242
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:20,520
that rival seller in the black market?

243
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:22,000
I've been trying.

244
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:24,280
They use different people
to sell the goods each time,

245
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:28,280
so we can't trace the mastermind.
We have no idea who they are.

246
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:30,480
You can't even find them!

247
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:31,640
Do I have to do it myself?

248
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,400
Ugh!

249
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,520
I understand,

250
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:38,520
Boss.

251
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:48,960
That Thatri is already
a big enough thorn in my side,

252
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:51,880
and now there's this mysterious enemy!

253
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:03,640
No one knows you work for me.

254
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:06,200
So, you are the perfect assets

255
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:09,320
to fan out and investigate who this person

256
00:24:10,560 --> 00:24:12,080
undercutting our prices is.

257
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,520
Yes, Boss.

258
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,800
We'll handle it.

259
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,440
But…

260
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:20,280
Thatri already knows I tricked him.

261
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:22,960
I shouldn't be out in the open.

262
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:25,320
Then head to the opium dens.

263
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:28,800
In Phuket, there's no better place
to gather intel than there.

264
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:32,600
Besides, Thatri will never suspect it.

265
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,400
I don't want to go.

266
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:36,120
That's an order.

267
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:39,120
We're short on men.
Everyone needs to pull their weight.

268
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,600
Yes, Boss.

269
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:42,920
Let's move.

270
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:07,440
At first, I was worried about
how I'd slip out to bring you intel.

271
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:10,320
Turned out he forced me out himself.

272
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:11,760
Still, it's quite concerning.

273
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:14,680
Anyone brave enough to undercut
a pirate like Zhang Gong Cheng

274
00:25:15,480 --> 00:25:17,040
must be someone extraordinary.

275
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:18,640
Let's put that matter aside for now.

276
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:20,920
How are things on your end?

277
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:22,640
As planned,

278
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:26,000
they spread the marked items,
and we busted them all.

279
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:28,520
Now we know exactly
who is involved, what they do,

280
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:30,760
and which merchants bought from them.

281
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:33,800
Except for Zhang Gong Cheng's big boss.

282
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:35,400
We still don't know who it is.

283
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,440
If you capture Zhang Gong Cheng,

284
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:40,280
finding the boss will be easy.

285
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:48,800
They kept the stolen goods in a warehouse

286
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,360
and will move them tomorrow.

287
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:53,200
You must take them down today.

288
00:25:53,280 --> 00:25:56,040
I've noted every single detail,
including the escape routes.

289
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:57,600
It's up to you now.

290
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:00,360
I must head back.

291
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:09,160
THERE ARE TWO ENTRANCES
THERE ARE THREE EXITS

292
00:26:21,440 --> 00:26:24,240
Do you know who's undercutting us yet?

293
00:26:24,840 --> 00:26:26,040
Still no clue, Boss.

294
00:26:45,320 --> 00:26:46,920
What about Colonel Nakamura?

295
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:49,880
He's waiting on the other side,
just like you planned.

296
00:26:51,760 --> 00:26:53,120
Then we wait for the signal.

297
00:26:59,720 --> 00:27:02,000
Wai. Did you find anything out?

298
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:04,760
Still no clue who is undercutting us.

299
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,520
Here you go.

300
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:10,600
I sent you out for intel,

301
00:27:10,680 --> 00:27:12,400
and you brought back liquor instead?

302
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:15,480
Well, I like it.

303
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:21,280
Hey, drink up.

304
00:27:23,440 --> 00:27:26,000
Wai. Have a drink with us.

305
00:27:27,120 --> 00:27:29,680
Later, man. I need
to use the bathroom first.

306
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:05,360
Everyone, move in.

307
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:13,760
Who the hell is setting off flares
in broad daylight?

308
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:15,520
Go check it out.

309
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:16,680
Yes, Boss.

310
00:28:36,840 --> 00:28:37,760
Where?

311
00:28:39,080 --> 00:28:40,680
I don't see anyone firing flares.

312
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:43,520
Could it just be kids playing around?

313
00:28:44,040 --> 00:28:45,640
He's getting too paranoid.

314
00:28:46,520 --> 00:28:48,920
What a waste of good drinking time.

315
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:57,400
-Hey!
-Let go!

316
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:01,280
I said let go!

317
00:29:04,560 --> 00:29:07,480
Freeze! Don't move! Drop your weapon!

318
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:48,040
Hold your fire!

319
00:30:00,520 --> 00:30:02,200
Zhang Gong Cheng…

320
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:04,280
It's finally over.

321
00:30:12,840 --> 00:30:14,440
Move it.

322
00:30:16,280 --> 00:30:17,800
Hurry up.

323
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:19,080
Walk.

324
00:30:19,600 --> 00:30:21,160
Move it. Faster.

325
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:23,120
Let me go!

326
00:30:23,200 --> 00:30:24,800
-Move it! Fast!
-I said let me go!

327
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:26,520
-Move out!
-Let go!

328
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:34,280
How is the situation, Thatri-san?

329
00:30:34,360 --> 00:30:35,200
All cleared.

330
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:38,920
We've recovered most of the stolen goods.

331
00:30:39,560 --> 00:30:41,080
As for the rest,

332
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:42,880
we'll get them back.

333
00:30:42,960 --> 00:30:45,200
We have the buyers' list.

334
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:48,280
What about Zhang Gong Cheng, Colonel?

335
00:30:49,920 --> 00:30:52,800
He's dead. His body is outside.

336
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:55,800
We'll collect it with the others later.

337
00:31:02,680 --> 00:31:04,120
Is something wrong, Chief?

338
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:07,280
I'll be right back.

339
00:32:12,480 --> 00:32:13,440
Die, you bastard.

340
00:32:58,800 --> 00:33:02,360
District Chief. Hang in there.

341
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:06,520
Help! Somebody help!

342
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:12,920
Don't fall asleep.

343
00:33:15,080 --> 00:33:16,240
Somebody help!

344
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:21,480
Doctor! Help! Open up, Doctor!

345
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:24,080
-Doctor!
-I hear you!

346
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:25,600
I'm coming!

347
00:33:25,680 --> 00:33:26,560
Jeez,

348
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,520
what's the rush?

349
00:33:27,600 --> 00:33:29,280
DOCTOR SOMSAK

350
00:33:29,360 --> 00:33:31,320
Oh, you again?

351
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:33,320
Did you bring in another stray dog?

352
00:33:33,920 --> 00:33:35,320
It's not a dog. It's a human.

353
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:38,400
It's the District Chief. He's been shot.

354
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:39,320
Hurry, come with me.

355
00:33:39,400 --> 00:33:41,120
Oh, really?!

356
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:42,920
-Where is he?
-Let me help.

357
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:44,080
Over here.

358
00:33:44,160 --> 00:33:46,280
DOCTOR SOMSAK

359
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:03,120
Tri. How's Bundit?

360
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:06,800
The doctor is working on him.
Try to relax, Sasi.

361
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:09,840
Why didn't you take him to the hospital?

362
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:13,679
The hospital in Phuket
lacks medicine and equipment,

363
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:16,679
and it's completely overcrowded.

364
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:19,719
He will receive much better care here.

365
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:23,719
As for medical supplies,

366
00:34:23,800 --> 00:34:26,760
the Japanese military
will provide full support.

367
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:31,280
I've also ordered my soldiers
to prepare for a blood transfusion.

368
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:34,120
Please don't worry.

369
00:34:34,960 --> 00:34:36,520
Thank you, Colonel.

370
00:34:37,239 --> 00:34:40,040
I can't help but worry about him.

371
00:35:08,200 --> 00:35:10,680
Is he going to be okay, Tri?

372
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:27,200
Rajit…

373
00:36:36,200 --> 00:36:37,640
You guys…

374
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:41,480
Why are you sleeping here?
Did something happen?

375
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:44,200
It's nothing.

376
00:36:44,760 --> 00:36:48,440
The District Chief was shot yesterday,

377
00:36:49,120 --> 00:36:51,520
so Uncle Ree and I
stayed up late watching over him.

378
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:54,760
I guess I was just exhausted
and dozed off.

379
00:36:56,640 --> 00:36:59,920
Then the rumors that the District Chief
was shot and nearly died

380
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:01,320
are true?

381
00:37:05,920 --> 00:37:08,320
And how is the District Chief doing now?

382
00:37:22,720 --> 00:37:25,360
He's stable for now,
but don't let your guard down.

383
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:27,200
Come get me if anything changes.

384
00:37:27,280 --> 00:37:28,320
Thank you.

385
00:37:28,400 --> 00:37:30,720
Thank you, Doctor.
I'll have someone walk you out.

386
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:31,840
Thank you.

387
00:37:32,440 --> 00:37:34,240
Nid, see the doctor out.

388
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:35,360
Yes, sir.

389
00:37:36,600 --> 00:37:38,200
This way, Doctor.

390
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:45,440
I feel so sorry for the District Chief.

391
00:37:45,520 --> 00:37:48,640
When I heard the news,
I didn't think it would be this bad.

392
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:54,720
But the doctor said he's stable now.
He'll pull through.

393
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:01,760
Hey. Sasi.

394
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:03,720
What's wrong?

395
00:38:04,560 --> 00:38:07,720
I'm just a bit dizzy.
I guess it's from staying up all night.

396
00:38:10,200 --> 00:38:12,360
Come sit over here.

397
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:14,000
Let's go.

398
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:22,960
Easy now.

399
00:38:26,520 --> 00:38:29,040
I'll fetch a damp cloth for you.

400
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:30,240
Thank you.

401
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,120
Are you feeling any better?

402
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:17,760
Yes.

403
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:27,040
No wonder. They used to be engaged.

404
00:39:27,120 --> 00:39:28,280
That explains it.

405
00:39:28,360 --> 00:39:31,280
Uncle Ree was being so sweet with her.

406
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:34,920
He never talks to me that way.

407
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,760
I'm so jealous!

408
00:39:38,360 --> 00:39:40,520
But she's already married
to the District Chief.

409
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:43,240
Old flames won't reignite,
will they, Rajit?

410
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:49,720
I'm sure Uncle Ree and Ms. Sasitorn

411
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:52,640
would never do anything immoral.

412
00:39:54,400 --> 00:39:57,680
True, he's not that kind of man.

413
00:39:58,480 --> 00:40:00,160
But even so,

414
00:40:00,240 --> 00:40:02,560
between Uncle Ree and her,

415
00:40:02,640 --> 00:40:04,280
do they still love each other?

416
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:06,080
That's food for thought.

417
00:40:06,920 --> 00:40:07,840
Huh?

418
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:11,440
You mean an emotional affair?

419
00:40:11,520 --> 00:40:13,600
-Oh no!
-Oh no!

420
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:15,640
-Uncle Ree.
-Uncle Ree.

421
00:40:26,080 --> 00:40:27,240
Rajit.

422
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:32,800
Is something the matter, Uncle Ree?

423
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:36,080
Sasi has to stay and care
for the Chief here for a few days.

424
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:37,520
I'm sorry to trouble you.

425
00:40:39,920 --> 00:40:44,040
Don't worry. I already had Jiam
prepare a room since last night.

426
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:46,360
Thank you.

427
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:55,040
Well? Is there anything else, Uncle Ree?

428
00:40:57,120 --> 00:40:58,400
I…

429
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:03,080
It's nothing.

430
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:07,280
If there's nothing else,
I'll take my leave.

431
00:41:08,280 --> 00:41:09,480
Mm.

432
00:41:11,040 --> 00:41:11,920
Let's go.

433
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:25,840
You coward. Why couldn't
you just speak up?

434
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:36,840
A one-winged bird can't fly alone,

435
00:41:38,960 --> 00:41:41,040
so I guess it's grounded forever.

436
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:09,560
This bird is born with one wing and leg.
It can never fly on its own,

437
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:11,800
not until it meets its other half.

438
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:26,120
The stars are beautiful.

439
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:30,160
I had no idea the stars out here
would be this breathtaking at night.

440
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:27,600
Please help me! Uncle Ree!

441
00:43:33,520 --> 00:43:35,840
Let's go, Rajit. Jump!

442
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:51,240
<i>Let me see the wound.</i>

443
00:44:37,760 --> 00:44:39,920
We lost men, supplies,

444
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:41,800
and my entire network!

445
00:44:41,880 --> 00:44:43,680
Everything is ruined!

446
00:44:43,760 --> 00:44:45,880
How could you be this incompetent?

447
00:44:45,960 --> 00:44:47,440
You can't entirely blame me.

448
00:44:47,520 --> 00:44:49,040
I was extremely careful.

449
00:44:49,120 --> 00:44:51,320
I never stay in one place for long

450
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:52,920
and constantly move.

451
00:44:54,120 --> 00:44:55,200
I'm also surprised

452
00:44:55,840 --> 00:44:57,920
they found our location.

453
00:44:58,600 --> 00:44:59,960
Could there be a mole among us?

454
00:45:00,960 --> 00:45:04,160
Everyone I brought in was strictly vetted

455
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:07,360
and tested multiple times.
It's impossible.

456
00:45:07,440 --> 00:45:09,000
Impossible?

457
00:45:09,080 --> 00:45:11,800
Then how did Thatri track you down
and raid the place?

458
00:45:11,880 --> 00:45:12,960
You idiot!

459
00:45:18,960 --> 00:45:20,520
I'll investigate this myself.

460
00:45:22,040 --> 00:45:25,520
Since no one suspects me yet,

461
00:45:26,160 --> 00:45:28,720
it shouldn't be hard
to root out the traitor.

462
00:45:29,320 --> 00:45:32,240
Once we find them, I'll kill them myself.

463
00:45:34,800 --> 00:45:36,480
I'll make them suffer horribly,

464
00:45:37,120 --> 00:45:38,440
even into their next life.

465
00:45:51,080 --> 00:45:53,160
Hang in there. Just a bit more.

466
00:46:17,960 --> 00:46:19,200
Thank you.

467
00:46:19,720 --> 00:46:21,960
I'm so lucky

468
00:46:22,800 --> 00:46:23,960
to have you by my side.

469
00:46:34,680 --> 00:46:38,400
My apologies, Mr. Thatri.
I forgot you were here.

470
00:46:45,040 --> 00:46:46,440
It's fine, District Chief.

471
00:46:47,320 --> 00:46:48,920
That's just how it is with newlyweds.

472
00:46:56,360 --> 00:46:58,120
How are you feeling, District Chief?

473
00:46:58,200 --> 00:47:00,120
I came as soon as I heard the news.

474
00:47:00,200 --> 00:47:02,360
It was quite severe, Ms. Fuangfah.

475
00:47:02,440 --> 00:47:03,840
Thank you so much.

476
00:47:04,800 --> 00:47:05,720
Honey,

477
00:47:06,560 --> 00:47:08,240
this is Ms. Fuangfah,

478
00:47:08,320 --> 00:47:10,280
Thatri's older cousin.

479
00:47:10,800 --> 00:47:14,200
And this is Sasitorn, my wife.

480
00:47:20,440 --> 00:47:21,760
I'll leave you to it then.

481
00:47:31,640 --> 00:47:32,520
Oh.

482
00:47:32,600 --> 00:47:35,000
I think I left something in the car.

483
00:47:35,080 --> 00:47:37,840
Please excuse me, District Chief, ma'am.

484
00:47:37,920 --> 00:47:39,320
Of course.

485
00:47:50,720 --> 00:47:52,280
Colonel, Wai.

486
00:47:52,880 --> 00:47:53,920
Are you here for the Chief?

487
00:47:55,920 --> 00:47:56,920
Yes.

488
00:47:57,000 --> 00:47:58,960
How is he doing?

489
00:47:59,920 --> 00:48:03,200
He's awake and can eat light meals now,
but he still has a fever.

490
00:48:03,880 --> 00:48:05,240
With his wife by his side,

491
00:48:05,320 --> 00:48:07,400
he'll be fine. He'll recover in no time.

492
00:48:07,480 --> 00:48:08,840
Wai…

493
00:48:15,400 --> 00:48:17,080
You're back, Ms. Fuang?

494
00:48:20,280 --> 00:48:21,360
Yes.

495
00:48:28,880 --> 00:48:32,000
Oh, Wai. Are you coming back to work here?

496
00:48:32,080 --> 00:48:33,520
Uh… no, ma'am.

497
00:48:33,600 --> 00:48:35,720
I'm just here to see the District Chief.

498
00:48:37,160 --> 00:48:39,400
Where are you going, Fuang?

499
00:48:39,960 --> 00:48:41,880
I just remembered some urgent work.

500
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:44,560
I must run, so I can get to my next task.

501
00:48:51,800 --> 00:48:52,680
We're almost done loading the goods.

502
00:48:52,760 --> 00:48:53,640
Good.

503
00:48:53,720 --> 00:48:56,800
We can finally plan
to eliminate Thatri for good.

504
00:48:56,880 --> 00:49:00,280
That damn Thatri.
I wish I could kill him right now.

505
00:49:08,840 --> 00:49:11,600
That's a shame. You just got here.

506
00:49:11,680 --> 00:49:13,200
I was going to ask you to stay for dinner.

507
00:49:13,800 --> 00:49:15,920
Another time, then. I'll go now.

508
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:17,000
Sure.

509
00:49:24,560 --> 00:49:26,440
Let's go see the Chief.

510
00:49:27,040 --> 00:49:28,160
Alright.

511
00:49:28,760 --> 00:49:29,880
I'll lead the way.

512
00:49:45,400 --> 00:49:46,440
Wai!

513
00:49:52,640 --> 00:49:54,560
You sure are quick like your name, Wai.

514
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:56,280
If you'd been slower,

515
00:49:56,880 --> 00:49:58,400
this blade would be all the way in.

516
00:50:07,360 --> 00:50:08,400
Stop!

517
00:50:15,400 --> 00:50:17,120
Good thing you're alive.

518
00:50:17,200 --> 00:50:19,400
I'll enjoy torturing you even more.

519
00:50:29,920 --> 00:50:31,120
Get up, Wai.

520
00:51:03,560 --> 00:51:05,280
This pearl is for you,

521
00:51:05,360 --> 00:51:06,960
in exchange for your life.

522
00:51:19,160 --> 00:51:20,560
What the hell are you doing?

523
00:51:29,600 --> 00:51:30,600
Wai?

524
00:51:31,360 --> 00:51:33,280
Wai. Hey you.

525
00:51:33,360 --> 00:51:34,480
Are you okay?

526
00:51:35,680 --> 00:51:36,840
Mr. Vijarn.

527
00:51:38,080 --> 00:51:39,160
Hang in there.

528
00:51:46,680 --> 00:51:48,880
So, you carry a gun, Mr. Vijarn?

529
00:51:50,520 --> 00:51:54,240
It's for self-defense.
During times of war,

530
00:51:54,320 --> 00:51:57,680
bandits and looters are everywhere.
I keep it close, even at home.

531
00:51:59,920 --> 00:52:01,440
I told Colonel Nakamura.

532
00:52:01,520 --> 00:52:04,520
He'll send men
to look after you. Rest easy.

533
00:52:04,600 --> 00:52:05,760
Thank you, sir.

534
00:52:06,480 --> 00:52:08,280
But there's one thing that bothers me.

535
00:52:09,600 --> 00:52:10,680
You mean

536
00:52:10,760 --> 00:52:13,360
how Zhang Gong Cheng found out
you betrayed him, right?

537
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:17,600
Yes, sir. After I signaled you
to bring the police,

538
00:52:18,200 --> 00:52:19,440
I never saw him again.

539
00:52:19,520 --> 00:52:21,440
He shouldn't have suspected me.

540
00:52:21,960 --> 00:52:23,200
True.

541
00:52:24,160 --> 00:52:27,840
And he ambushed you right after
you left Som Song Saeng house.

542
00:52:27,920 --> 00:52:30,560
How could he track
your movements so precisely?

543
00:52:32,040 --> 00:52:35,040
Could there be a mole among us,
Mr. Thatri?

544
00:52:37,800 --> 00:52:40,440
If so, there is one person on my mind.

545
00:52:41,320 --> 00:52:42,360
Who?

546
00:52:42,960 --> 00:52:44,320
Ms. Fuangfah.

547
00:52:46,760 --> 00:52:48,560
You're talking nonsense, Wai.

548
00:52:48,640 --> 00:52:50,640
Ms. Fuangfah working
with Zhang Gong Cheng?

549
00:52:51,720 --> 00:52:55,560
I know it sounds unbelievable,
but the shoes Ms. Fuangfah was wearing

550
00:52:56,200 --> 00:52:58,720
are identical to the ones worn
by Zhang Gong Cheng's boss.

551
00:52:58,800 --> 00:53:01,880
<i>Gold shoes with such a unique,</i>
<i>embroidered pattern,</i>

552
00:53:02,840 --> 00:53:04,600
<i>I doubt many people</i>
<i>in Phuket would wear them.</i>

553
00:53:04,680 --> 00:53:07,040
And at Som Song Saeng house today,

554
00:53:07,640 --> 00:53:10,440
Ms. Fuangfah was
the only acquaintance I ran into.

555
00:53:10,520 --> 00:53:12,400
If someone tipped off Zhang Gong Cheng,

556
00:53:13,160 --> 00:53:15,160
she's the most suspicious one.

557
00:53:18,040 --> 00:53:19,600
Suspicious as she is,

558
00:53:19,680 --> 00:53:22,720
we have no evidence to prove
Fuang is Zhang Gong Cheng's boss.

559
00:53:23,520 --> 00:53:25,080
We can't do anything anyway.

560
00:53:26,360 --> 00:53:28,600
What about the pearl, Mr. Thatri?

561
00:53:28,680 --> 00:53:30,600
Could that be used as evidence?

562
00:53:34,400 --> 00:53:36,200
It looks like a regular pearl to me.

563
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:38,320
How could it be evidence?

564
00:53:39,160 --> 00:53:42,160
Here's the thing. At first,

565
00:53:42,240 --> 00:53:46,280
I didn't believe Wai either,
but it makes sense now.

566
00:53:46,960 --> 00:53:50,640
As for this pearl, it's different
from the ones usually found in Phuket.

567
00:53:50,720 --> 00:53:52,880
It's a freshwater pearl.

568
00:53:52,960 --> 00:53:54,040
How do you know that?

569
00:53:54,120 --> 00:53:56,000
By its color.

570
00:53:56,080 --> 00:53:58,480
Freshwater pearls have a duller luster
and are less beautiful

571
00:53:58,560 --> 00:53:59,840
than saltwater ones.

572
00:53:59,920 --> 00:54:01,720
People in Phuket only use saltwater pearls

573
00:54:01,800 --> 00:54:04,760
because they're locally sourced
and fetch a better price.

574
00:54:05,920 --> 00:54:09,200
Ms. Fuangfah is the only person
who imports freshwater pearls.

575
00:54:09,280 --> 00:54:12,520
Why would she specifically
use freshwater pearls?

576
00:54:13,600 --> 00:54:17,080
Ms. Fuangfah once told me
that when we do something wrong,

577
00:54:17,160 --> 00:54:19,280
a pearl can atone for our sins.

578
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:39,080
But using a saltwater pearl
would be a waste of money.

579
00:54:39,760 --> 00:54:42,280
So she orders
freshwater ones just for this.

580
00:55:05,200 --> 00:55:06,440
Boss…

581
00:55:06,520 --> 00:55:08,120
I already know everything.

582
00:55:15,280 --> 00:55:17,760
Here, take this.

583
00:55:18,280 --> 00:55:20,160
Use it to lay low in Langkawi for a while.

584
00:55:20,240 --> 00:55:23,520
The Japanese influence
hasn't reached there yet.

585
00:55:23,600 --> 00:55:26,400
Come back once the war is over.

586
00:55:27,880 --> 00:55:29,280
And what about you, Boss?

587
00:55:30,400 --> 00:55:33,880
No one suspects me. Even if they do,

588
00:55:33,960 --> 00:55:35,960
there's no evidence.

589
00:55:37,880 --> 00:55:41,080
But you messed up by failing to kill Wai.

590
00:55:42,640 --> 00:55:45,840
Thatri and the Japanese will
turn Phuket upside down hunting you.

591
00:55:53,880 --> 00:55:55,240
Thank you, Boss.

592
00:55:55,320 --> 00:55:59,480
Go now. I'll have someone
smuggle you out before dawn tomorrow.

593
00:56:18,040 --> 00:56:20,080
<i>You two used to be engaged, after all.</i>

594
00:56:20,160 --> 00:56:21,680
<i>It's normal to worry about him.</i>

595
00:56:21,760 --> 00:56:23,000
You knew about this?

596
00:56:24,400 --> 00:56:25,960
I brought something back for you.

597
00:56:26,040 --> 00:56:27,120
What is it?

598
00:56:33,600 --> 00:56:34,960
The police are probably here.

599
00:56:35,040 --> 00:56:36,480
Turn yourself in, Fuang.

600
00:56:38,400 --> 00:56:39,880
Oh my God!

601
00:56:40,720 --> 00:56:41,800
Fuang!

602
00:56:41,880 --> 00:56:44,040
Where did Rajit go, Auntie Jiam?

603
00:56:44,120 --> 00:56:45,440
She went with Ms. Fuang.

604
00:56:46,560 --> 00:56:48,360
Aunt Fuang, are you lost?

605
00:56:48,440 --> 00:56:50,720
Shut your mouth! You never stop talking!

606
00:56:50,800 --> 00:56:52,280
Why do you have to do this?

607
00:56:52,360 --> 00:56:53,800
Go to hell, Rajit!

608
00:57:23,400 --> 00:57:26,080
Subtitle translation by:
Khathathong Thongtumlueng
